    "sources:Content_en.txt": {
      "fingerprint": "c903007a88fce976e9d42af5a0b6435667e8dc4ea12bb14e12c07ff781f620b4",
      "kind": "sources",
      "status": "needs_reference",
      "issues": [
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: - In the **Kesavananda Bharati case (1973)**, the Supreme Court held the Preamble is a **part of the Constitution**.",
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: - **Fundamental Duties (Article 51A, Part IVA):** added by the **42nd Amendment, 1976**, on the recommendation of the **Swaran Singh Committee**; inspired by the **USSR**. Originally 10 duties; the **11th** was added by the **86th Amendment, 2002** (parent/guardian to provide education to child aged 6–14).",
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: - **Judicial review** and the **Basic Structure doctrine** (Kesavananda Bharati, 1973) keep Parliament's amending power in check.",
        "Fetch official supporting evidence for: The **106th Constitutional Amendment (2023)** — the *Nari Shakti Vandan Adhiniyam* — provides one-third reservation for women in the Lok Sabha and State Assemblies. It will take effect after the next census and delimitation. When you study Articles 330/332 (reservation provisions), remember this living link — exams increasingly connect static Articles with recent amendments."
      ],
